# Competency question: "Which properties frame a hypothesis test, an effect size, an interval,
# a prediction, a diagnostic, a fitted model, and an inference run?" Exercises the remaining
# result/evaluation object properties across the paradigm-result and model-evaluation layers:
# a math:HypothesisTest weighs an alternative (math:alternativeHypothesis) and reports an
# effect size (math:effectSize); a math:EffectSize names its contrast (math:effectSizeContrast)
# and standardization scale (math:effectSizeScale); an interval names its bounds
# (math:hasIntervalBound) and coverage/mass (math:confidenceLevel / math:credibleMass); a
# math:Prediction names its target (math:predictionTarget); a math:ModelDiagnostic anchors to
# the fit (math:diagnosticFor) via a method (math:diagnosticMethod); a fitted model posits an
# assumption (math:modelAssumption); and a math:InferenceRun follows a plan
# (math:usedAnalysisPlan). The query projects each PREDICATE, scoped to the framed subjects and
# the math: namespace. Over the fixture the answer is exactly the thirteen framing edges.
PREFIX math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/>
PREFIX ex:   <http://example.org/math/>

SELECT ?subject ?prop ?object WHERE {
    VALUES ?subject { ex:test ex:es ex:ci ex:cri ex:pred ex:diag ex:fit ex:run }
    ?subject ?prop ?object .
    FILTER(STRSTARTS(STR(?prop), "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/"))
}
ORDER BY ?subject ?prop ?object
